Exercise: sa-perms-review (chapter 7 lab)

Work on servera, with sudo or as root.

People
 1. The group analysts, with GID 36000.
 2. dana and evan, both members of analysts (supplementary group).
 3. visitor, who is not in analysts.

Team directory
 4. /srv/analysis, owned by root, group analysts, mode 2770 (so new files
    inherit the group).
 5. /srv/analysis/summary.txt, created by dana, containing the line
    "Quarterly summary". It belongs to dana and group analysts and has
    mode 660.
 6. /srv/analysis/bin/report.sh, owned by dana, group analysts, mode 750.
    Any short script will do.

Drop box
 7. /srv/dropbox, a directory every user can write to, where users can
    delete only their own files (mode 1777).

Exceptions for visitor (use ACLs, not group membership)
 8. visitor may read summary.txt, and nothing more.
 9. visitor may pass through /srv/analysis (execute only). New files created
    in /srv/analysis must grant visitor read access by default.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-perms-review
